{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["With clay — on the inside." "And with pitch — on the outside, so that the water would not enter it." "And she placed it at the river's bank — that is, near the bank of the river. And she hid it well, so that those walking along the bank of the river would not be able to see the ark, but one bathing inside the river could see it. For Yocheved did not enter the river to conceal it thoroughly on all sides, and that is why Pharaoh's daughter, who was bathing inside the river, saw it, but her maidens, who were walking along the bank, could not see it."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:40:39.877438827Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}